  <article class="content-page section-space shell"><h1>Care comes first.</h1>
    <div class="mt-8 notice"><strong>New or sudden loss of movement needs urgent veterinary assessment.</strong><p>Do not delay treatment to measure, print, fit or buy a chair.</p></div>
    <h2>Ask about suitability before fit</h2><p>A rear-support cart is not appropriate for every dog or every stage of care. Ask a veterinarian or rehabilitation professional about diagnosis, front support, posture, skin health and an appropriate activity plan.</p>
    <h2>A chair is part of a care plan</h2><p>Supervision, comfort checks and rest matter. Follow the treating professional's instructions. The project does not prescribe a universal exercise schedule or offer medical treatment through a size selector.</p>
